## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates understanding of AWS-native DevOps practices applied to SAP ABAP environments, requiring knowledge of both AWS supply chain security principles and SAP transport management realities.

## Key Concepts
- AWS CodePipeline, CodeBuild, CodeArtifact integration
- SAP ABAP/NetWeaver transport and change management
- IAM least privilege and environment segregation
- Cryptographic signing with AWS Signer and KMS
- Deployment governance and automated rollback strategies

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "codebuild:StartBuild",
        "codebuild:BatchGetBuilds"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:codebuild:*:*:project/abap-build-*"
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "codeartifact:PublishPackageVersion",
        "codeartifact:ReadFromRepository"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:codeartifact:*:*:repository/abap-addons/*"
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "signer:StartSigningJob",
        "signer:GetSigningProfile"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:signer:*:*:signing-profile/abap-signing-*"
    }
  ]
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Zero-trust for SAP GUI/RFC in a multi-region, multi-account AWS setup, with password rotation and auditable access, tests real-world security posture and automation.

## Key Concepts

- SSO/SAML integration for SAP access
- JIT access with STS and MFA
- SAP auth mapping to IAM roles and SCPs
- Secrets Manager rotation for SAP passwords
- Private networking with VPC Endpoints
- Observability via CloudTrail and CloudWatch

## Code Example

```javascript
{
  "AWSTemplateFormatVersion": "2010-09-09",
  "Resources": {
    "TempSAPAccessRole": {
      "Type": "AWS::IAM::Role",
      "Properties": {
        "AssumeRolePolicyDocument": {
          "Version": "2012-10-17",
          "Statement": [{
            "Effect": "Allow",
            "Principal": { "AWS": "*" },
            "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
          }]
        },
        "Policies": [{
          "PolicyName": "TempSAPAccess",
          "PolicyDocument": {
            "Version": "2012-10-17",
            "Statement": [
              {"Effect": "Allow", "Action": ["sts:AssumeRole"], "Resource": "*"}
            ]
          }
        }]
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale this model across many SAP landscapes and tenants?
- What changes would you make to strengthen audit trails for non-repudiation?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ABAC-based cross-account SAP access controls, per-SAP-object mapping, JIT elevation, and PrivateLink in a realistic multi-account SAP deployment.

## Key Concepts
- ABAC using aws:PrincipalTag & aws:RequestTag
- Cross-account trust with SCPs
- JIT elevation with STS MFA
- PrivateLink for SAP endpoints

## Code Example
```javascript
// ABAC trust policy (illustrative)
{
  Version: '2012-10-17',
  Statement: [{
    Effect: 'Allow',
    Principal: { AWS: 'arn:aws:iam::SHARED:root' },
    Action: 'sts:AssumeRole',
    Condition: { StringEquals: { 'aws:PrincipalTag.sap_obj': '<OBJ_ID>' } }
  }]
}
```
```javascript
// Example access policy predicate
{
  Effect: 'Allow',
  Action: ['sap:Read', 'sap:Write'],
  Resource: '*',
  Condition: { StringEquals: { 'aws:RequestTag.sap_role': '<ROLE>' } }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate ABAC mappings at scale across accounts?
- What failure modes exist with ABAC in SAP, and mitigations?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests a beginner's ability to design a practical, auditable maintenance workflow using familiar AWS services with least-privilege access.

## Key Concepts

- AWS Systems Manager Run Command
- IAM roles with trust relationships and least privilege
- CloudWatch Logs and CloudTrail for audit trails
- AWS SSO integration for role assumption
- Minimal IaC (Terraform) to create roles and SSM associations

## Code Example

```terraform
# Terraform snippet creating cross-account SAPOperator role and IAM policy
provider "aws" { region = "us-east-1" }

# Role
resource "aws_iam_role" "sap_operator" {
  name = "SAPOperator"
  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17",
    Statement = [{
      Effect = "Allow",
      Principal = { AWS = "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT_ID:saml-provider/AWS_SSO" },
      Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
    }]
  })
}

# Policy
resource "aws_iam_policy" "sap_operator_policy" {
  name = "SAPOperatorPolicy"
  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17",
    Statement = [
      { Effect = "Allow", Action = ["ssm:SendCommand","ssm:ListCommands","ssm:DescribeInstanceInformation"], Resource = "*" },
      { Effect = "Allow", Action = ["logs:CreateLogGroup","logs:CreateLogStream","logs:PutLogEvents"], Resource = "*" }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "attach" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.sap_operator.name
  policy_arn = aws_iam_policy.sap_operator_policy.arn
}
```

```terraform
# SSM association to run healthcheck on SAP EC2
data "aws_ssm_document" "run_shell" { name = "AWS-RunShellScript" }

resource "aws_ssm_association" "healthcheck" {
  name            = data.aws_ssm_document.run_shell.name
  instance_id     = "<SAP_EC2_INSTANCE_ID>"
  parameters = {
    commands = ["bash /usr/local/bin/healthcheck.sh"]
  }
}
```

